hadiths[33]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15760","Sakan ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah informed me, that his father informed him, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying voluntary prayer at night on a journey on the back of his mount wherever it faced with him."
"15761","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd al-Taymi, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave and said: What grave is this? They said: The grave of so-and-so woman. He said: Why did you not inform me? They said: You were sleeping, and we disliked to wake you. He said: Do not do so; call me for your funerals. He lined up over her and prayed."
"15762","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you see a funeral, stand until it passes you. Or he said: Stop until it passes you. He said: And Ibn Umar, when he saw a funeral, would stand until it passed him, and when he went out with a funeral, he would turn his back to the graves."
"15763","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, from Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you sees the funeral and is not walking with it, let him stand until it passes him or is placed."
"15764","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, that a man from Banu Fazarah married a woman for two sandals, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted his marriage."
"15765","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I heard Nafi' say: Abd Allah ibn Umar used to report from Amir ibn Rabi'ah, that he used to say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees the funeral, let him stand when he sees it until it leaves him behind, if he is not following it."
"15766","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) countless times using the siwak while fasting. And Abd al-Rahman said: Countless times cleaning his teeth while fasting."
"15767","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: I heard Shu'bah, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amir narrating from his father, that a man married a woman for two sandals. He said: She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: That is for him? He said: Are you pleased for yourself and your wealth for two sandals? She said: Yes. Shu'bah said: I said to him: As if he permitted that? He said: As if he permitted it. Shu'bah said: Then I met him and he said: Are you pleased for yourself and your wealth for two sandals? She said: I saw that. He said: And I see that."
"15768","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah narrating from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching, saying: Whoever sends blessing upon me, the angels keep sending blessing upon him as long as he sends blessing upon me, so let a servant do little of that or much."
"15769","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Asim ibn Ubayd Allah informed me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me there will be rulers who pray the prayer at its time and delay it from its time, so pray it with them. If they pray it at its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and for them. And if they delay it from its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and against them. Whoever leaves the community dies a death of ignorance, and whoever breaks the covenant and dies breaking the covenant will come on the Day of Resurrection with no proof. I said to him: Who informed you of this report? He said: Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah informed me, from his father Amir ibn Rabi'ah, Amir ibn Rabi'ah informing from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15770","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Amir ibn Rabi'ah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees the funeral, let him stand until it leaves him behind or is placed."
"15771","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"15772","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying voluntary prayers on the back of his mount in every direction."
"15773","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Amir ibn Rabi'ah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see a funeral, if you are not walking with it, stand for it until it leaves you behind or is placed. He said: And Ibn Umar would sometimes go ahead of the funeral and sit, until when he saw it approaching he would stand until it was placed, and sometimes it concealed him."
"15774","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on his mount wherever it faced with him."
"15775","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, from Amir ibn Rabi'ah, conveying to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you see the funeral, stand for it until it leaves you behind or is placed."
"15776","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) using the siwak countless times while fasting."
"15777","Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one sends blessing upon me but the angels send blessing upon him as long as he sends blessing upon me, so let a servant do little of that or much."
"15778","Shu'ayb ibn Harb narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Ubayd Allah informed us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah narrating from his father, and he was a Badr veteran, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sends blessing upon me, and he mentioned it."
"15779","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal ibn Hilal ibn Asad al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: My father, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from his father, that a man from Banu Fazarah married a woman for two sandals, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted it."
"15780","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, and he was a Badr veteran, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send us in an expedition. O my son, we had no provision but a loan of dates, and he would divide it handful by handful until it became date by date. He said: I said to him: O father, what would a date avail you? He said: Do not say that, O my son, for after we lost it we needed it."
"15781","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Asim ibn Ubayd Allah informed me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers after me who pray the prayer at its time and delay it, so pray it with them. If they pray it at its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and for them. And if they delay it from its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and against them. Whoever leaves the community dies a death of ignorance, and whoever breaks the covenant and dies breaking the covenant will come on the Day of Resurrection with no proof. I said: Who informed you of this report? He said: Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah informed me, from his father Amir ibn Rabi'ah, informing from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15782","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: From Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for following up between them removes poverty and sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron."
"15783","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, that Amir ibn Rabi'ah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glorifying while upon the mount, nodding with his head toward whichever direction it faced, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not do that in the obligatory prayer."
"15784","Abu al-Nadr and Husayn narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, meaning Ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies with no obedience upon him dies a death of ignorance, and if he casts it off after binding it upon his neck, he will meet Allah, blessed and exalted is He, with no proof for him."
"15785","No, let no man be alone with a woman unlawful to him, for their third is Satan, except a mahram, for Satan is with the one and farther from the two."
"15786","Whoever is displeased by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed, he is a believer. Husayn said: After binding it upon his neck."
"15787","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Aswad said: And sometimes Sharik mentioned, from Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for following up between them increases lifespan and provision, and removes sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron."
"15788","Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, narrating from Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, conveying, and once he said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for following up between them removes sins and poverty as the bellows removes dross. Sufyan said: It does not contain his father."
"15789","Ya'qub narrated to us, the nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: Amir ibn Rabi'ah, one of Banu Adi ibn Ka'b, informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the funeral, stand for it until it leaves you behind."
"15790","Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Umayyah ibn Hind ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, he said: Amir ibn Rabi'ah and Sahl ibn Hunayf set out intending washing. He said: They set out seeking concealment. He said: Amir put down a wool cloak that was upon him, and I looked at him and struck him with my eye. He descended into the water to wash. He said: I heard gurgling for him in the water, so I came to him and called him three times and he did not answer me. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: He came walking and waded into the water, as if I see the whiteness of his shanks. He said: He struck his chest with his hand then said: O Allah, remove from him its heat and its cold and its fatigue. He said: He stood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees in his brother, or in himself, or in his wealth what pleases him, let him bless him, for the evil eye is true."
"15791","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Yahya ibn Jurjah narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abd Allah ibn Amir narrated to me, he said: Amir saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on the back of his mount."
"15792","Yunus ibn Muhammad and Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from his father, Surayj said: Ibn Rabi'ah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umrah to Umrah is expiation for the sins and wrongs between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise."
